# Knowledge Check Edit Slide lock (do not regress)

Anthony (2026-11-01): Edit on a Knowledge Check still showed leftover “Test your understanding…” on-screen text that is not on the slide, while the stem and choices (e.g. “Base olefins” → “Lower olefins”) could not be changed without regenerate.

`npm test` must stay green (`src/lib/knowledgeCheckOst.test.ts`).

## Invariants (code, not comments)

- **Edit Text shows the question.** For quiz / multiple-choice / multiple-answers / true-false / `knowledge-check`, Edit Slide does **not** render the leftover OST RichTextEditor. [`isQuizKnowledgeCheckType`](src/lib/knowledgeCheckOst.ts) gates that in [`App.tsx`](src/App.tsx).
- **Stem and choices are the fields.** [`knowledgeCheckEditQuestions`](src/lib/knowledgeCheckOst.ts) reads `interactions[0]` first (player source), then `data`. [`applyKnowledgeCheckEdits`](src/lib/knowledgeCheckOst.ts) writes **both** so Save updates the slide the learner sees.
- **Correct answers are togglable.** Radio for single-select; checkbox for multiple-answers (`setKnowledgeCheckCorrect`). Do not require Regenerate to change a word or the keyed answer.
- **Keep the player layout.** Do not put “Test your understanding” back on the KC canvas.

## How to change this

Change the helpers and add a failing test first. Do not “fix” Edit by putting the stem into on-screen text.
